# GeeksHub Frontend Audit
> Full audit of all files in `src/` — what exists, what's a stub, and what's missing.

---

## 🔴 Critical — Broken / Non-functional

### 1. [CourseMaterials.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/CourseMaterials.tsx) — Hardcoded Stub
**File:** [src/components/pages/CourseMaterials.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/CourseMaterials.tsx) (22 lines)

**Problem:** The entire component is a hardcoded placeholder. It renders only one hardcoded link (`/courses/:courseId/files/123`) regardless of which course is selected. It doesn't use `useFiles()`, doesn't fetch real files, and doesn't filter by tab type.

**What it should do:**
- Call `useFiles({ courseId, type: undefined })` to list all materials for the course
- Render each file as a clickable card linking to `/courses/:courseId/files/:fileId`
- Show file type badges (Slides, Notes, Homeworks, Past Papers)
- Show loading skeleton and empty state

---

### 2. [CourseNotes.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/CourseNotes.tsx) — Complete Stub
**File:** [src/components/pages/CourseNotes.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/CourseNotes.tsx) (11 lines)

**Problem:** Entire body is a static string: `"Notes View Content"`. No logic, no data fetching.

**What it should do:**
- Call `useFiles({ courseId, type: "Notes" })` and display the results
- Same file list treatment as CourseMaterials but pre-filtered to Notes only

---

### 3. [CourseExams.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/CourseExams.tsx) — Complete Stub
**File:** [src/components/pages/CourseExams.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/CourseExams.tsx) (11 lines)

**Problem:** Body is a static string: `"Past Exams View Content"`. No logic, no data fetching.

**What it should do:**
- Call `useFiles({ courseId, type: "Past Papers" })` and display results

---

### 4. [FileViewer.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/viewer/FileViewer.tsx) — Hardcoded Demo PDF
**File:** [src/components/viewer/FileViewer.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/viewer/FileViewer.tsx) (line 57)

**Problem:**
```ts
content: { location: { url: "https://documentcloud.adobe.com/view-sdk-demo/PDFs/Bodea Brochure.pdf" } }
```
Every single file — regardless of what's selected — loads the same Adobe demo brochure PDF. The `file.downloadUrl` field exists in the [File](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/types/domain.ts#150-164) type but is never used.

**What it should do:**
- Use `file.downloadUrl` when available
- Fall back gracefully (error state) when `downloadUrl` is `undefined`
- Show a placeholder UI for non-PDF file types (`.pptx`, `.docx`, `.xlsx`)

---

### 5. [AssistantPanel.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx) — Fake AI with `setTimeout`
**File:** [src/components/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx) (line 155–164)

**Problem:** The AI response is a 1-second `setTimeout` that always returns a templated string. The "Notes" tab shows a `"Coming Soon"` button.

**What it should do:**
- Replace `setTimeout` with a real `POST /api/assistant/chat` call
- Read `fileId` from route params and pass it in the request body
- The Notes tab should be a real `<textarea>` that saves to `POST /api/me/notes`
- The filename shown at the bottom (`"Introduction to Algorithms.pdf"`) is hardcoded; it should use the actual current file title from context/params

---

### 6. [UserUploads.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/UserUploads.tsx) — "View" Link Hardcoded to File `123`
**File:** [src/components/pages/UserUploads.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/UserUploads.tsx) (line 165)

**Problem:**
```tsx
to={`/courses/${file.courseId}/files/123`}
```
Every approved file's "View" button navigates to the same hardcoded file ID `123`, ignoring the actual file from the request.

**What it should do:** Link to the actual approved `fileId` corresponding to the request (requires the backend to return a `fileId` on approved [FileRequest](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/types/domain.ts#169-189) objects).

**Also missing:** The search bar (`input` on line 111) has no `onChange` handler — it does nothing.

---

## 🟠 High Priority — Missing Core Features

### 7. Authentication Context — No Auth Provider
**Files:** Entire app has no `AuthProvider` or protected route wrapper.

**Problem:** 
- [AppShell.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx) shows a hardcoded `"D"` avatar and `"Deena"` / `"student@uni.edu"` 
- Dashboard says `"Welcome back, Deena"` (hardcoded at line 755)
- `DEMO_USER_ID = "u1"` is hardcoded in [Dashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Dashboard.tsx) and [UserUploads.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/UserUploads.tsx)
- Anyone can access `/admin` directly — there is no role check
- [authService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/services/authService.ts) has real sign-in/sign-up methods but they return a `user` object nobody stores

**What's needed:**
- An `AuthContext` / `useAuth()` hook that holds the authenticated user
- Protected route wrappers for `/` (requires login) and `/admin` (requires `role === ADMIN`)
- User profile in sidebar reading from context (`user.displayName`, `user.avatarInitials`)
- The [signIn](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/services/authService.ts#12-39)/[signUp](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/services/authService.ts#40-62) flows should call `setUser()` in context on success

---

### 8. `/path` Route — Navigates to 404
**File:** [src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx) (line 96)

**Problem:** The sidebar has a "My Path" nav item linking to `/path`, but this route doesn't exist in [router.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/lib/router.tsx). Clicking it causes a `RouteError`.

**What's needed:** Either add a route + page for `My Path`, or temporarily remove the nav item.

