### 10. [Settings.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Settings.tsx) — Imports from a Stale File
**File:** [src/components/pages/Settings.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Settings.tsx) (line 16)

**Problem:**
```ts
import { majors, years, userRequests } from "@/lib/data";
```
This imports from `@/lib/data` which is a **different file** from `@/mock/mock-db`. The `majors` in [lib/data.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/lib/data.ts) are likely plain strings (legacy), while the canonical mock has them as `Major[]` objects. This is an inconsistency / potential runtime error.

**Also:** All settings state is local only — language is saved to `localStorage`, but nothing else persists. The "Saved" badge always shows (hardcoded at line 118).

---

### 11. Dashboard — Hardcoded Metrics and Activity Data
**File:** [src/components/pages/Dashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Dashboard.tsx)

**Problem:**
- Metric cards (Study Hours, Courses Active, Completion Rate, XP Earned) are hardcoded static arrays (lines 36–41)
- Weekly Activity bar chart uses a hardcoded static array (lines 44–52)
- Course progress bars use `Math.random()` (line 826) — they change on every render
- `COURSE_META` lookup map (line 635) uses different course IDs (`cs201`, `cs301`, `eng201`) from the mock DB course IDs (`cs101`, `cs102`, `math201`)

