## 🔵 Low Priority — Polish & Future Work

### 19. [FileViewer.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/viewer/FileViewer.tsx) — Non-PDF Files Not Handled
Files of type `Slides` (`.pptx`), `Homeworks` (`.docx`/`.xlsx`) cannot be displayed in Adobe's PDF SDK. There's no fallback for non-PDF content (download button, unsupported format message).

### 20. [AppShell.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx) — "Activate Pro" Button is Decorative
The "Upgrade" / "Activate Pro" card in the sidebar (line 217) has no `onClick` handler.

### 21. [Settings.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Settings.tsx) — Non-functional Toggles
`compactMode` and `reduceMotion` state changes do nothing — there's no CSS class applied, no context updated. These need to be wired to a theme context or CSS variable.

### 22. [Dashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Dashboard.tsx) — Tasks Stored Only in `localStorage`
**File:** [src/hooks/useTasks.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/hooks/useTasks.ts)

Tasks live in `localStorage` only — no backend persistence. This is fine for now but tasks are cleared when localStorage is cleared and don't sync across devices.

### 23. [Dashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Dashboard.tsx) — Recent Courses Links Don't Navigate Correctly
Line 805: `to={'/courses?course=${course.id}'}` — the [Courses](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Documents/Programming%20projects/GeeksHub/GeeksHub/src/components/pages/Courses.tsx#17-339) page reads `selections.course` from state, not from URL query params. Clicking "View all → course card" doesn't pre-select the course. The URL query param `?course=...` goes unread.

### 24. Missing `404 / Not Found` Page
There is no catch-all route for unknown URLs. The router has `errorElement: <RouteError>` on some routes but no `path="*"` catch-all. Navigating to `/unknown` shows nothing / blank.

### 25. No Global Loading / Error Boundary
Outside of per-route `errorElement`, there is no top-level error boundary. A React render error in any component unmounts the whole app silently.

